            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Search the web for the most relevant recent papers (2024-2026) on: (1) encoding-based jailbreak defenses for LLMs, specifically any that use curriculum learning or progressive training; (2) compositional generalization applied to adversarial robustness; (3) any paper specifically training lightweight classifiers to be robust against encoded/ciphered jailbreak attacks. I need to assess whether the novelty claim of \"curriculum-structured training for encoding-robust safety classifiers\" has been preempted. Use WebSearch if available, otherwise report what you know. Keep findings concise - just paper titles, key ideas, and how they relate."
            }
